      "id": 14476,
      "title": "Solid fuel use for household cooking: Country and regional estimates for 1980–2010",
      "description": "95% Confidence Intervals for the years 1990, 2000, and 2010 are given in the Supplemental Material, Table S3. To give one example: The world's households primarily relying on solid fuels for cooking declined from 62% to 41% between 1980 and 2010. The 95% confidence interval for 1980 is from 58% to 66% and for 2010 from 37% to 44%.\n\nCountries are grouped by WHO region and income category (WHO 2012e; see Supplemental Material, Table S2).",
